-- title:
--   Parity of vdet describes Γ₂ at all levels
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison at the prime $q$. Fixed data: a squarefree level $N$, primes $q \ne q'$ neither dividing $N$, both at least $5$, a natural number $D$ divisible by $2Nqq'$, and a valuation subring $A_2$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ in its set of nonunits (`LiesOverPrime`), assumed to have the isometry property that every element of its decomposition subgroup over $\mathbb{Q}$ preserves the valuation.
--
--   Definite side. Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and such that the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]$ is division at exactly the finite place above $q'$ (`IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`); submodules $\Lambda_1$, $R_1$ of it with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$), and $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$; a finite idele $n_1$ lying in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $q$; the hypotheses `hS₁`, `hnorm₁`, `hsq₁` and `hlaws₁` stating respectively that $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1, n_1) = R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nq$, is stable under conjugation by $n_1$, that shifting by $n_1$ is an involution on its class set, and that the Hecke operators on the edge and vertex class sets satisfy the commutation and degeneracy laws packaged in `ClassSetHeckeLaws` (four clauses, summarised here).
--
--   Indefinite side and moduli tower. Rationals $a, b$ with $a > 0$ or $b > 0$ such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b]$ is division exactly at the places above $q$ and $q'$, and a maximal order $\Lambda$ in it; a field $Fbar$ that is a curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in the sense of `IsCurveOver` and essentially of finite type over it; a scheme $X$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathbb{Z}[1/D]$ together with a base point $\overline{s}$ and a point map $pt$ assigning to each fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure over a ring $S$ an $S$-point of $X$; the hypotheses `pt_iso`, `pt_pullback`, `pt_surjective`, `pt_injective` expressing that $pt$ is constant on isomorphism classes, compatible with base change, and bijective on geometric points of algebraically closed fields — that is, the four non-universal clauses of coarse representability. Further: a curve model $\mathfrak{M}$ of $Fbar$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak{M}}$ from $\mathfrak{M}.C$ to the fibre product of $\pi_X$ and $\overline{s}$ compatible with the structure maps, semilinear Galois actions $gal$ and $galT$, a Hecke tower $\mathbb{T}$ of function fields indexed by the primes away from $q$ and $q'$, Atkin–Lehner semilinear automorphisms $W$, $WT$, and a witness $tw$ of `ModuliTowerWitnessD` tying the moduli description to the tower.
--
--   Local data at $q$. A height one prime $v_2$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathbb{Z}$ containing $q$; an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\iota_2$ from $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]$ into $2 \times 2$ matrices over the rational closure $\mathrm{ratClosure}(A_2)$ inside the completion of $A_2$'s valuation, together with the induced projective representation $\rho_2$ of units; a pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi_2$ whose image in the completion is $q$, with the holomorphic ring of $\rho_2$ a domain; elements $s_2(\ell) \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]^\times$ and finite ideles $sf_2(\ell)$, for $\ell$ ranging over primes away from $q$, $q'$, satisfying `hs₂`: away from $q$ the local component of $sf_2(\ell)$ is $s_2(\ell) \otimes 1$, at $q$ it is $1$, the quotient of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ by $sf_2(\ell)$ lies in the level Hecke set for $\Lambda_1$ and $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1, n_1)$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_2(\ell)) = \ell$.
--
--   The groups. $\Gamma_2$ is a family of subgroups of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]^\times$ indexed by $\mathrm{Option}$ of the away primes, subject to `hΓ₂0`: $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ consists of those $x$ lying in $\mathrm{awayUnits}(R_1, v_2)$ — the intersection over all $w \ne v_2$ of the preimages under localisation of the closure of the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$ — with $\mathrm{padicValRat}_q(\mathrm{nrd}\,x)$ even; and `hΓ₂ℓ`: $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)$ is the intersection of $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ with its conjugate by $s_2(\ell)$. Elements $w_2$, $\overline{w}_2$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]^\times$ indexed by the same set, with `hw₂` asserting $w_2(\mathrm{none}) \in \mathrm{awayUnits}(R_1, v_2)$ of reduced norm $q$, and $w_2(\mathrm{some}\,\ell) \in \mathrm{awayUnits}(\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1, sf_2(\ell)), v_2)$ of reduced norm $q$, and `hwbar₂` asserting (both at level $\mathrm{none}$ and at each $\ell$) that $\overline{w}_2$ has reduced norm $q'$, lies in the local box units away from $v_2$ and from the places above $q'$, and normalises the local boxes of the relevant order and of $\Lambda_1$ at every place $\ne v_2$.
--
--   Galois and character data. A homomorphism $dIso_2$ from the decomposition subgroup of $A_2$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ into isometric automorphisms of the completion, inducing the natural action; a character $\chi$ of that decomposition subgroup with values in $\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb{Z}/2)$, trivial on inertia, nontrivial on any Frobenius at $q$, and with kernel described by fixing the $q^2$-elements of the residue field of $A_2$.
--
--   Integral models and the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation. A complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_0$ of characteristic zero with uniformiser $\pi$, residue cardinality $q$ and $(q) = (\pi)$, realised inside $\mathrm{ratClosure}(A_2)$ as a fraction-ring base with $\pi \mapsto \varpi_2.\varpi$, with $N$ invertible; an unramified extension $Onr$ with Frobenius $Fr$ satisfying $Fr(x) \equiv x^q \pmod{\pi}$, complete, with maximal ideal $(\pi)$, integral over $\mathcal{O}_0$ modulo $\pi$ and Henselian-type root-lifting; a homomorphism $vdet$ from $GL_2(\mathrm{ratClosure}(A_2))$ to $\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb{Z})$ characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(n)$ precisely when $\det g$ is a unit of $\mathcal{O}_0$ times $\pi^n$; a map $\psi_0 : Onr \to$ completion with valuation at most $1$ and compatible with $\mathcal{O}_0$; the conditions `h𝒪₀` identifying the image of $\mathcal{O}_0$ with the valuation-$\le 1$ part and `hrk` a rank-one approximation property. Then: integral coarse moduli schemes $\mathcal{X}_0 \to \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal{O}_0$ and $\mathcal{Y}_0(\ell) \to \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal{O}_0$ for fake elliptic curves with and without extra level $\ell$ (with $\mathcal{X}_0$ flat, separated, locally of finite type and quasi-compact over the base), degeneracy maps $d_{0}$, $d_{1}$ over the base inducing forgetting the extra level and passing to the $\ell$-isogenous curve, and Atkin–Lehner involutions $ar$, $arbar$ over the base realising the quotients at $q$ and at $q'$ on points. Finally formal uniformisation maps $\Theta$ and $\Theta T(\ell)$ from the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ with Drinfeld's functor $\Omega$ into the nilpotent points of $f_0$ and of $g_0(\ell)$, and the hypothesis `hCD` (eleven clauses, summarised here) asserting: naturality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta T(\ell)$; invariance of $\Theta$ under the twisted action of $\mathrm{awayUnits}(R_1, v_2)$ and of $\Theta T(\ell)$ under the twisted action of $\mathrm{awayUnits}(R_1, v_2) \cap s_2(\ell)\,\mathrm{awayUnits}(R_1, v_2)\,s_2(\ell)^{-1}$; that over an algebraically closed field with $\pi$ nilpotent, $\Theta$ and $\Theta T(\ell)$ are surjective and have fibres exactly the orbits of those groups; the universal property of $\Theta$ and of $\Theta T(\ell)$ among such equivariant maps; compatibility of $\Theta T(\ell)$ with $d_0$ and, after the twisted action of $s_2(\ell)$, with $d_1$; and compatibility of $\Theta$ with $ar$ via the Frobenius twist by $1$ on the $Onr$-coordinate and with $arbar$ via the twisted action of $\overline{w}_2(\mathrm{none})$.
--
--   The conclusion is a sixfold conjunction. First, there exists $z$ in $\mathrm{awayUnits}(R_1, v_2)$ and a scalar $c \in \mathrm{ratClosure}(A_2)$ with $\iota_2(z) = c \cdot 1$ as a $2 \times 2$ matrix and $vdet(\iota_2(z)) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(2)$. Second, there exists $w$ in $\mathrm{awayUnits}(R_1, v_2)$ with $vdet(\iota_2(w)) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(1)$. Third, for all $x \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]^\times$: $x \in \Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ if and only if $x \in \mathrm{awayUnits}(R_1, v_2)$ and $\mathrm{toAdd}(vdet(\iota_2(x)))$ is even. Fourth, for every away prime $i$ there exists $z$ in $\mathrm{awayUnits}(R_1, v_2) \cap s_2(i)\,\mathrm{awayUnits}(R_1, v_2)\,s_2(i)^{-1}$ and a scalar $c$ with $\iota_2(z) = c \cdot 1$ and $vdet(\iota_2(z)) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(2)$. Fifth, for every away prime $i$ there exists $w$ in that same intersection with $vdet(\iota_2(w)) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(1)$. Sixth, for every away prime $i$ and every $x \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]^\times$: $x \in \Gamma_2(\mathrm{some}\,i)$ if and only if $x$ lies in that intersection and $\mathrm{toAdd}(vdet(\iota_2(x)))$ is even. Here $\iota_2$ is applied to units through the induced map on unit groups.
--
--   This is the translation step, at the prime $q$, from the reduced-norm description of the arithmetic group $\Gamma_2$ and its level-$\ell$ subgroups to the description by the parity of the $\pi$-adic valuation of the determinant under the local embedding $\iota_2$, together with the existence of a central element of determinant valuation $2$ and of an element of determinant valuation $1$ inside each of these groups. It feeds the construction of the Mumford embedding realising the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve at $q$.
